reason=Incident label events reconcile CI mode. New .github/workflows/incident-label-ci.yml (119 lines) acts on a labeled/unlabeled event for expedited-incident-response ONLY, on a same-repo PR. It selects the newest pull_request ci.yml run of that PR (by number) on its current head; with none listed yet it stops green. Otherwise it at once creates an in-progress ci-green check run on the head (the ruleset requires ci-green from the GitHub Actions app, which this token creates check runs as), so the stale verdict stops counting, including after a COMPLETED expedited run. It then cancels an unfinished run and waits, holds ci-green again, and re-runs; the re-run's own ci-green replaces the hold. Its concurrency group is shared only by incident label events. auto-enable-merge.yml gains one gate conjunct plus 4 comment lines, inserted with no existing line changed: it skips the unlabeled event of that label, so it cannot race the hold and merge on the stale green. That only narrows when auto-merge arms. Any other label skips the new job at the job level (no runner), and ci.yml's triggers are unchanged. 124 lines added, 0 removed or modified against merge base 356b21ae; no check removed; the required-check set unchanged. The reusable-check-matrix omission half was split out: it reduces a quality gate (maintainer tier).
